Hmmm...
Those are two very good points.  You might be able
in theory to work around them (not me - I don't have
the patience, and by the way, thank you for all the
work you put in to generate this data), by only
considering games that are played after completing
the challange or ignoring it, though I guess that
decreases the amount of statistics you have even
more.

As for players having multiple goals, that's a very also
a valid point, though you might be able to filter things
by not considering players who have ascended a
pacifist/illiterate/etc, or those who died in more than
50% of the possible different ways.   Obviously this
will get rid of the "serial ascenders", data.

Actually, this leads me to another thought.  Your
definition of "serial ascender" is solid (though I
don't consider myself a serial ascender even though
I qualify by your metric), and I wonder if you can
say things about how many serials (or regulars)
have ascended with which conducts - just to
figure out which are the easiest.

Anyway.

How about this idea:  NAO is great for people who
have ascended, but if you want to measure how
well people who have never ascended (or have a hard
time) with the various classes, then look at the data
from devnull, but *only* consider those who won the
